text: ['At the beginning of your upkeep, if Genesis is in your graveyard, you may pay {2}{G}. If you do, return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Destroy all creatures target opponent controls. Draw a card for each creature destroyed this way.', 'Destroy target permanent.', 'Each player may put an artifact, creature, enchantment, or land card from their hand onto the battlefield.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', "Search target opponent's library for a creature card and put that card onto the battlefield under your control. Then that player shuffles.", 'When Imperial Recruiter enters the battlefield, search your library for a creature card with power 2 or less, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'You may play lands from your graveyard.']
flavor: ['"First through the Riftstone was Genesis—and the world was lifeless no more."\\n—*Scroll of Beginnings*', '"I have seen entire civilizations rise and fall. You mortals are but dust to me."\\n—Sorin Markov', 'Amidst the darkest ashes grow the strongest seeds.', 'At the academy, "show and tell" too often becomes "run and hide."', 'By the year 208, Cao Cao commanded more than 1,000 experienced generals and a million infantry, cavalry, and naval troops.', 'The smallest seed of regret can bloom into redemption.']
